    "input": {
      "prompt": "A realistic isolated 3D game-prop concept study, one single ancient riverbank oak growing almost SIDEWAYS, seen in a clean side profile with a little depth. Entire object visible against pure white, no scenery or floor plane. The ROOT COLLAR and a short thick leaning trunk exist ONLY at the extreme LEFT of the image. That trunk continuously curves into an enormous low horizontal crooked S-shaped over-water limb, extending to the RIGHT across about 80 percent of the whole silhouette. The long lateral limb is the dominant structure, several times longer than the height of the root stump. Its thick broad irregular wood makes a gentle knee and another organic shallow bend; it gradually tapers rather than ending in a blunt sawn cut. A broad unequal Y-fork sweeps diagonally above and alongside the main limb; further sideways branches split recursively into many smaller irregular twigs, some drooping down. Natural oak branch collars and gnarled junctions. Offshoot angles and lengths vary organically, with obvious negative space. Sparse irregular broadleaf sprays and small leafy clusters distributed along real connected twig networks; airy broken canopy, never a dome or roof. A few dark green hanging moss threads and short vines underneath the wood. Rough deeply fissured dark brown bark, moss in damp crevices, healed knots, weathered gray ridges. Photoreal natural tree anatomy, detailed sculptural wood, restrained forest greens. No upright central tree, no umbrella canopy, no radial octopus roots, no straight railing, no repeated upward prongs, no counted fork pattern, no round lollipop foliage balls, no floating detached pieces, no water, no snake, no text. Wide composition with clear margins around the whole root-to-tip tree.",
